WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.268
-Bernie Sanders won

00:00:02.268 --> 00:00:04.503
the Nevada caucus
in a landslide on Saturday

00:00:04.503 --> 00:00:07.007
and, now, some pundits
in the Democratic establishment

00:00:07.007 --> 00:00:08.975
are panicking
about the possibility

00:00:08.975 --> 00:00:11.077
that he might be
the Democratic nominee.

00:00:11.077 --> 00:00:12.979
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:12.979 --> 00:00:17.616
[ Suspenseful theme plays ]
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:17.616 --> 00:00:19.585
Bernie has now won
the popular vote

00:00:19.585 --> 00:00:21.320
in the first three
primary contests,

00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:22.821
making him
the clear front-runner,

00:00:22.821 --> 00:00:25.191
and, now, Politico is reporting
that Bernie sanders

00:00:25.191 --> 00:00:27.827
has sent the Democratic
establishment into panic mode.

00:00:27.827 --> 00:00:29.962
And you can tell
because the general tenor

00:00:29.962 --> 00:00:33.166
of the coverage on cable news
has gone something like this...

00:00:33.166 --> 00:00:34.734
-NBC News projects

00:00:34.734 --> 00:00:37.503
Bernie Sanders
the winner in Nevada.

00:00:37.503 --> 00:00:39.072
-What the [bleep] is going on?!

00:00:39.072 --> 00:00:41.007
[ Laughter ]

00:00:41.007 --> 00:00:42.374
[ Applause ]

00:00:42.374 --> 00:00:44.144
-Pundits across cable news

00:00:44.144 --> 00:00:46.012
have been freaking out
about Bernie's rise.

00:00:46.012 --> 00:00:48.214
For example, you might remember
that, after Bernie won

00:00:48.214 --> 00:00:51.050
the popular vote in Iowa
and again in New Hampshire,

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:52.852
the story wasn't
that he was winning,

00:00:52.852 --> 00:00:56.289
but that, if you used pundit
math, he was actually losing.

00:00:56.289 --> 00:00:58.858
-I don't understand how Bernie
is considered a front-runner.

00:00:58.858 --> 00:01:01.360
In New Hampshire,
52% of voters wanted

00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:05.664
either Pete Buttigieg
or Amy Klobuchar or Joe Biden.

00:01:05.664 --> 00:01:07.000
Moderates are winning.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:10.169
-Why wasn't
Buttigieg's win in Iowa

00:01:10.169 --> 00:01:11.704
a bigger banner headline?

00:01:11.704 --> 00:01:14.240
He also has upset Bernie Sanders
in both states.

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:15.341
-The story of the night:

00:01:15.341 --> 00:01:18.010
Amy Klobuchar now
in third place.

00:01:18.010 --> 00:01:20.413
-The story of the Sanders
campaign, so far, this year,

00:01:20.413 --> 00:01:22.882
is how much ground he's lost
from four years ago.

00:01:22.882 --> 00:01:24.917
-That's right:
By winning states,

00:01:24.917 --> 00:01:26.519
Bernie is actually
losing ground.

00:01:26.519 --> 00:01:27.754
[ Laughter ]
You see,

00:01:27.754 --> 00:01:29.288
as all expert pundits know,

00:01:29.288 --> 00:01:31.223
you don't wanna win
the first two.

00:01:31.223 --> 00:01:32.625
That's a rookie mistake,

00:01:32.625 --> 00:01:35.962
wherein you come off as needy
or, as the kids would say,

00:01:35.962 --> 00:01:37.763
thirsty.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:37.763 --> 00:01:40.666
You wanna throw everyone off
by losing a bunch of states,

00:01:40.666 --> 00:01:42.435
playing it cool,
off to the side,

00:01:42.435 --> 00:01:44.103
until someone finally says,

00:01:44.103 --> 00:01:46.538
"Who's that fellow
with zero delegates?"

00:01:46.538 --> 00:01:47.873
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:47.873 --> 00:01:49.542
No, seriously.

00:01:49.542 --> 00:01:53.813
[ Applause ]

00:01:53.813 --> 00:01:55.381
No, seriously, who is that?

00:01:55.381 --> 00:01:58.050
[ Laughter ]
Oh! Alright.

00:01:58.050 --> 00:01:59.452
See, according to the pundits,

00:01:59.452 --> 00:02:01.320
you don't actually win the first
two states, like Bernie did.

00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:02.689
You wanna follow
the Joe Biden path:

00:02:02.689 --> 00:02:04.623
Come in fourth in Iowa,
fifth in New Hampshire,

00:02:04.623 --> 00:02:05.891
and a distant second in Nevada.

00:02:05.891 --> 00:02:06.960
And, on top of all that,

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:08.828
just wander over
during a crucial debate

00:02:08.828 --> 00:02:10.229
[ Laughter ]
and give the front-runner

00:02:10.229 --> 00:02:11.497
a hug, you know.

00:02:11.497 --> 00:02:13.465
That's the first time Biden
ever hugged someone

00:02:13.465 --> 00:02:15.067
from an angle where
they could see him coming.

00:02:15.067 --> 00:02:17.169
[ Laughter and ohs ]
And, not only

00:02:17.169 --> 00:02:18.837
[ Laughter and applause ]
did some pundits insist

00:02:18.837 --> 00:02:20.540
that Bernie wasn't actually
the front-runner

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:21.841
after winning
the first two states,

00:02:21.841 --> 00:02:24.977
they also created an elaborate
mythology in their heads

00:02:24.977 --> 00:02:27.547
where Bernie was only winning
because the so-called moderates

00:02:27.547 --> 00:02:29.682
were supposedly
splitting the vote.

00:02:29.682 --> 00:02:31.651
And they kept insisting that,
if the moderates

00:02:31.651 --> 00:02:33.385
would just coalesce
around one candidate,

00:02:33.385 --> 00:02:35.454
that candidate could be Bernie.

00:02:35.454 --> 00:02:37.323
-Bernie Sanders may have
eked out the most votes

00:02:37.323 --> 00:02:38.824
in Iowa and New Hampshire,

00:02:38.824 --> 00:02:40.726
but if you look
at the numbers more closely,

00:02:40.726 --> 00:02:42.761
it shows a candidate
hitting a ceiling.

00:02:42.761 --> 00:02:44.697
If you look
at the combined percentages

00:02:44.697 --> 00:02:46.432
among the centrist candidates,

00:02:46.432 --> 00:02:48.568
they do much better
than the progressives.

00:02:48.568 --> 00:02:49.969
-When you add up the totals,
though,

00:02:49.969 --> 00:02:53.273
for Pete Buttigieg,
Amy Klobuchar, and Joe Biden,

00:02:53.273 --> 00:02:54.973
when you add them up last night,

00:02:54.973 --> 00:02:58.544
that's more than half the
electorate backing a moderate.

00:02:58.544 --> 00:03:00.379
-Buttigieg and Klobuchar
and Biden

00:03:00.379 --> 00:03:03.116
split the moderate vote,
with their combined percentage

00:03:03.116 --> 00:03:06.219
overwhelming that of Sanders,
who got 26%.

00:03:06.219 --> 00:03:08.421
-That's right: If you just
combine the votes of Buttigieg,

00:03:08.421 --> 00:03:10.223
Biden, and Klobuchar,
you can beat Bernie.

00:03:10.223 --> 00:03:11.757
[ Laughter ]
Now, all you have to do is

00:03:11.757 --> 00:03:14.793
find a way to genetically
combine them into one candidate,

00:03:14.793 --> 00:03:16.662
called the
Klobu-Biden-Butti-char.

00:03:16.662 --> 00:03:19.499
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:19.499 --> 00:03:21.733
It's that's easy.
And then, all --

00:03:21.733 --> 00:03:23.202
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:03:23.202 --> 00:03:24.971
And then, every time
you ask it a question,

00:03:24.971 --> 00:03:26.272
it has the same answer.

00:03:26.272 --> 00:03:28.140
What should we do
about healthcare?

00:03:28.140 --> 00:03:31.277
-We must step forward
into the future.

00:03:31.277 --> 00:03:32.444
-I'm from Minnesota.

00:03:32.444 --> 00:03:35.047
-CornPop was a bad dude.

00:03:35.047 --> 00:03:36.382
-Alright.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:36.382 --> 00:03:38.183
But the reality is
that most actual voters

00:03:38.183 --> 00:03:39.252
don't think like pundits.

00:03:39.252 --> 00:03:40.686
They don't divide candidates

00:03:40.686 --> 00:03:42.789
into a so-called liberal lane
and a moderate lane.

00:03:42.789 --> 00:03:44.890
In fact, polls have shown
that the top second choice

00:03:44.890 --> 00:03:46.692
among Biden voters
is actually Bernie.

00:03:46.692 --> 00:03:48.461
Polls have shown
that Democratic voters

00:03:48.461 --> 00:03:50.863
are overwhelmingly satisfied
with choices.

00:03:50.863 --> 00:03:52.565
They don't divide them up
into lanes.

00:03:52.565 --> 00:03:54.033
They like them each
for their own reasons.

00:03:54.033 --> 00:03:55.435
They like Bernie
for his consistency

00:03:55.435 --> 00:03:56.669
on issues like health care.

00:03:56.669 --> 00:03:58.837
They like Warren
for taking on big fights

00:03:58.837 --> 00:04:00.406
against special interests,
like Wall Street.

00:04:00.406 --> 00:04:02.808
They like Biden for his
eight years as Obama's VP.

00:04:02.808 --> 00:04:05.211
They like Buttigieg for his
youthful charm and charisma.

00:04:05.211 --> 00:04:07.280
They like Klobuchar
for her record in the Senate.

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:08.414
And they like Bloomberg

00:04:08.414 --> 00:04:10.116
because he pays people
to like him.

00:04:10.116 --> 00:04:11.684
[ Laughter ]

00:04:11.684 --> 00:04:14.287
Still, before Nevada,
many in the media were desperate

00:04:14.287 --> 00:04:15.855
to avoid calling Sanders
the front-runner

00:04:15.855 --> 00:04:17.390
and, in fairness,
only two states,

00:04:17.390 --> 00:04:18.957
both of them mostly white,
had voted.

00:04:18.957 --> 00:04:21.260
In fact, even Bernie bristled
at the question

00:04:21.260 --> 00:04:22.695
of whether he was
the front-runner

00:04:22.695 --> 00:04:24.330
during a town hall on CNN.

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:27.399
-I think it was right before
New Hampshire primary,

00:04:27.399 --> 00:04:30.203
I asked you, after Iowa,
if you considered yourself

00:04:30.203 --> 00:04:31.837
the Democratic front-runner.

00:04:31.837 --> 00:04:35.574
Now, after New Hampshire,
do you?

00:04:35.574 --> 00:04:37.977
-Who cares?
[ Laughter ]

00:04:37.977 --> 00:04:40.146
-If Bernie gets elected,
his inauguration

00:04:40.146 --> 00:04:42.515
is just gonna be
a four-hour open house.

00:04:42.515 --> 00:04:43.750
[as Sanders]
Stop by, don't stop by.

00:04:43.750 --> 00:04:45.217
There'll be cheese and crackers,
but, you know,

00:04:45.217 --> 00:04:46.752
maybe eat before you come.

00:04:46.752 --> 00:04:48.688
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:48.688 --> 00:04:50.089
[ Cheering ]
Say what you will --

00:04:50.089 --> 00:04:52.592
[ Applause ]

00:04:52.592 --> 00:04:54.260
[ Whistling ]
Say what you will about the guy,

00:04:54.260 --> 00:04:55.661
but he does not care
about status.

00:04:55.661 --> 00:04:59.031
He has one suit that he irons
by running it over

00:04:59.031 --> 00:05:00.133
with his car, I guess.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:00.133 --> 00:05:02.535
He shoots lay-ups with two hands

00:05:02.535 --> 00:05:04.270
and he's been photographed
in the middle seat in coach

00:05:04.270 --> 00:05:06.939
and that is the only time
he's been centrist.

00:05:06.939 --> 00:05:08.875
[ Laughter ]
But even

00:05:08.875 --> 00:05:11.644
the pundits and Bernie himself
cannot deny his clear status

00:05:11.644 --> 00:05:14.046
as the front-runner
after an overwhelming victory

00:05:14.046 --> 00:05:16.215
in Nevada on Saturday,
the first diverse state

00:05:16.215 --> 00:05:17.650
to vote in the primary,

00:05:17.650 --> 00:05:20.485
in which Sanders seemed to win
virtually every demographic.

00:05:20.485 --> 00:05:21.854
-Sanders, indeed, won

00:05:21.854 --> 00:05:23.655
a smashing,
across-the-board victory,

00:05:23.655 --> 00:05:25.191
according to our entrance poll.

00:05:25.191 --> 00:05:27.126
He won among men and women,

00:05:27.126 --> 00:05:29.395
college graduates
and non-college graduates,

00:05:29.395 --> 00:05:31.964
liberals
and moderates/conservatives,

00:05:31.964 --> 00:05:33.666
union and nonunion members,

00:05:33.666 --> 00:05:37.103
people who decided early
and people who decided late.

00:05:37.103 --> 00:05:38.705
In short, Sanders crushed it.

00:05:38.705 --> 00:05:40.005
[ Laughter ]
-Take a look here among

00:05:40.005 --> 00:05:42.208
self-described moderate or
conservative Democrats.

00:05:42.208 --> 00:05:44.510
That's a third
of this electorate in Nevada.

00:05:44.510 --> 00:05:45.711
This is what you're seeing.

00:05:45.711 --> 00:05:47.280
Sanders is actually leading.

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:49.314
-NBC/Wall Street Journal
poll asked,

00:05:49.314 --> 00:05:51.784
"Who are you most enthusiastic
or comfortable about,

00:05:51.784 --> 00:05:53.719
when it comes to the
Democratic nominee?"

00:05:53.719 --> 00:05:56.021
Bernie Sanders leads with 65%.

00:05:56.021 --> 00:05:59.158
-He was powered by young voters,
Hispanic voters,

00:05:59.158 --> 00:06:01.794
very liberal, and those
who supported Medicare for All.

00:06:01.794 --> 00:06:04.330
-Damn, he won union voters,
nonunion voters,

00:06:04.330 --> 00:06:05.731
young voters, Hispanic voters,

00:06:05.731 --> 00:06:07.633
men, women, liberals,
and conservatives.

00:06:07.633 --> 00:06:09.435
And, based on this photo,
he did well

00:06:09.435 --> 00:06:11.170
with former vice presidents
over 70.

00:06:11.170 --> 00:06:12.838
[ Laughter ]
And, yet, still,

00:06:12.838 --> 00:06:15.541
cable news reacted with shock
at Bernie's success in Nevada.

00:06:15.541 --> 00:06:17.343
For example,
as results were coming in

00:06:17.343 --> 00:06:20.179
and it was clear that
young voters and people of color

00:06:20.179 --> 00:06:21.848
were going overwhelmingly
for Sanders,

00:06:21.848 --> 00:06:23.549
one anchor at a caucus site

00:06:23.549 --> 00:06:26.018
audibly sighed
as she reported the results.

00:06:26.018 --> 00:06:28.387
-[dully]
Largely, people of color.

00:06:28.387 --> 00:06:31.657
Of those,
the majority are Latino

00:06:31.657 --> 00:06:36.261
and they are clearly,
at least from eyeballing it,

00:06:36.261 --> 00:06:37.929
[sigh] strongly in favor

00:06:37.929 --> 00:06:39.332
[ Laughter ]
of Bernie Sanders,

00:06:39.332 --> 00:06:41.500
with Joe Biden coming in second.

00:06:41.500 --> 00:06:43.970
-[laughing]
Oh, my God, with the sigh!

00:06:43.970 --> 00:06:47.473
[ Applause ]
She's reporting on Bernie
winning a caucus site

00:06:47.473 --> 00:06:48.841
the way you tell your parents

00:06:48.841 --> 00:06:51.310
why your dip[bleep] boyfriend
got fired from his job.

00:06:51.310 --> 00:06:52.544
[ Laughter ]

00:06:52.544 --> 00:06:55.347
[dully] "He, uh, well,
he was usin' the copier

00:06:55.347 --> 00:06:57.282
and, well, from eyeballin' it,

00:06:57.282 --> 00:06:59.051
it looks like he, uh,

00:06:59.051 --> 00:07:01.520
[sigh] he photocopied his ass

00:07:01.520 --> 00:07:02.554
and put it up
in the break room."

00:07:02.554 --> 00:07:05.091
[ Laughter and applause ]
And then --

00:07:05.091 --> 00:07:08.627
[ Cheering ]

00:07:08.627 --> 00:07:10.028
And then, prominent

00:07:10.028 --> 00:07:11.497
[ Whistling ]
Democratic strategists
and pundits

00:07:11.497 --> 00:07:13.532
started spinning out on live TV.

00:07:13.532 --> 00:07:16.302
James Carville, for example,
has been showin' up nonstop

00:07:16.302 --> 00:07:18.804
on MSNBC, warning
that nominating Bernie

00:07:18.804 --> 00:07:20.673
would destroy the party
and even suggesting that

00:07:20.673 --> 00:07:23.175
Russian President Vladimir Putin
was rooting for him.

00:07:23.175 --> 00:07:26.345
-It's gonna be the end of days,
so I'm scared to death.

00:07:26.345 --> 00:07:27.579
I really am.

00:07:27.579 --> 00:07:30.516
There's a certain part
of the Democratic Party

00:07:30.516 --> 00:07:31.817
that wants us to be a cult.

00:07:31.817 --> 00:07:34.153
I'm not interested
in being in a cult.

00:07:34.153 --> 00:07:36.889
I'm 75 years old.

00:07:36.889 --> 00:07:39.959
I'm just not
a very culty person.

00:07:39.959 --> 00:07:41.160
I'm 75 years old.

00:07:41.160 --> 00:07:42.662
Why am I here, doin' this?

00:07:42.662 --> 00:07:44.997
Because I am scared to death.
That's why.

00:07:44.997 --> 00:07:46.399
The happiest person right now --

00:07:46.399 --> 00:07:50.302
It's about 1:15 Moscow time.

00:07:50.302 --> 00:07:52.438
This thing is goin' very well
for Vladimir Putin.

00:07:52.438 --> 00:07:53.639
I promise you.

00:07:53.639 --> 00:07:55.707
He's probably stayin' up,
watchin' us right now.

00:07:55.707 --> 00:07:56.708
How you doin', Vlad?

00:07:56.708 --> 00:07:58.277
[ Laughter ]
-Alright.

00:07:58.277 --> 00:07:59.678
He's not watching,
but, if he was,

00:07:59.678 --> 00:08:02.214
he'd probably think this was
a public access puppet show.

00:08:02.214 --> 00:08:03.282
[ Laughter ]

00:08:03.282 --> 00:08:04.950
Seriously, James Carville
always looks like

00:08:04.950 --> 00:08:07.152
he was released naked
into a Louisiana Goodwill

00:08:07.152 --> 00:08:09.254
and given five minutes
to pick an outfit.

00:08:09.254 --> 00:08:10.790
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:08:10.790 --> 00:08:12.324
[ Giggles ]

00:08:12.324 --> 00:08:13.925
[as Carville]
How this hat look on me?

00:08:13.925 --> 00:08:15.895
How's this hat look on me, bad?
I'll take it.

00:08:15.895 --> 00:08:18.164
It's all squashed up
like a bug on my head? Yeah.

00:08:18.164 --> 00:08:19.564
Like it's completely
lost its shape?

00:08:19.564 --> 00:08:21.067
Alright. I'll take it.

00:08:21.067 --> 00:08:23.035
[ Laughter ]
And, just as a reminder

00:08:23.035 --> 00:08:24.069
of Carville's track record:

00:08:24.069 --> 00:08:26.571
In 2008, he said
then-Senator Barack Obama

00:08:26.571 --> 00:08:28.507
was unelectable
and attacked him to the point

00:08:28.507 --> 00:08:30.909
where even Obama hit back
and said James Carville

00:08:30.909 --> 00:08:32.845
is well-known
for spouting off his mouth

00:08:32.845 --> 00:08:34.580
without always knowing
what he's talking about.

00:08:34.580 --> 00:08:37.816
In fact, Obama was specifically
responding to this comment

00:08:37.816 --> 00:08:39.352
Carville made
about Hillary and Obama --

00:08:39.352 --> 00:08:40.419
and this is a real quote --

00:08:40.419 --> 00:08:42.754
"If she gave him one
of her cojones,

00:08:42.754 --> 00:08:43.855
they'd both have two."

00:08:43.855 --> 00:08:44.990
[ Laughter and ohs ]
Alright.

00:08:44.990 --> 00:08:47.393
I'm havin' trouble
following the logic here.

00:08:47.393 --> 00:08:48.894
So that means

00:08:48.894 --> 00:08:51.163
[laughing] she was starting
with three cojones?

00:08:51.163 --> 00:08:53.632
[ Laughter ]

00:08:53.632 --> 00:08:54.967
Yet, somehow, that wasn't even

00:08:54.967 --> 00:08:56.635
the most unhinged response
to Bernie's win.

00:08:56.635 --> 00:08:59.872
Chris Matthews actually compared
Bernie's victory in Nevada

00:08:59.872 --> 00:09:02.708
to the Nazi invasion of France
during World War II.

00:09:02.708 --> 00:09:05.611
-I'm reading last night
about the fall of France

00:09:05.611 --> 00:09:08.380
in the summer of 1940
and the general, Reynaud,

00:09:08.380 --> 00:09:11.384
calls up Churchill and says,
"It's over."

00:09:11.384 --> 00:09:13.052
And Churchill says,
"How can it be?

00:09:13.052 --> 00:09:14.887
You got the greatest army
in Europe.

00:09:14.887 --> 00:09:16.087
How can it be over?"

00:09:16.087 --> 00:09:17.289
He said, "It's over."

00:09:17.289 --> 00:09:19.691
So I had
that suppressed feeling.

00:09:19.691 --> 00:09:22.394
I can't be as wild as Carville,
but he is damn smart

00:09:22.394 --> 00:09:24.196
and I think he's damn right
on this one.

00:09:24.196 --> 00:09:26.832
-As a general rule, anytime
a man of Matthews' age

00:09:26.832 --> 00:09:28.667
starts a sentence with,
"I was reading last night

00:09:28.667 --> 00:09:30.536
about the fall of France
in 1940,"

00:09:30.536 --> 00:09:32.705
that's your queue
to exit the conversation.

00:09:32.705 --> 00:09:33.772
[ Laughter ]

00:09:33.772 --> 00:09:35.307
He's like your senile grandpa,

00:09:35.307 --> 00:09:36.709
screaming into the phone
on FaceTime:

00:09:36.709 --> 00:09:38.210
"They banned me
from the golf course

00:09:38.210 --> 00:09:39.445
for not fixin' my divots!

00:09:39.445 --> 00:09:41.981
This is just like 1940,
when the Nazis...!"

00:09:41.981 --> 00:09:43.815
[ Laughter and applause ]
Alright, alright.

00:09:43.815 --> 00:09:45.117
Talk to ya later, Grandpa.

00:09:45.117 --> 00:09:48.053
[ Cheering and applause ]
And, somehow --

00:09:48.053 --> 00:09:49.354
[laughing] Somehow,

00:09:49.354 --> 00:09:51.456
[ Whistle ]
this isn't the most insane thing

00:09:51.456 --> 00:09:52.758
Matthews has said about Bernie.

00:09:52.758 --> 00:09:54.126
After Bernie's win
in New Hampshire,

00:09:54.126 --> 00:09:56.696
you might recall, Matthews went
on another deranged tear,

00:09:56.696 --> 00:09:58.764
that had somethin' to do
with Communists

00:09:58.764 --> 00:10:00.632
executing him in Central Park
or something.

00:10:00.632 --> 00:10:03.469
It was so incoherent,
his fellow anchor Chris Hayes

00:10:03.469 --> 00:10:05.171
had to chime in
to offer some sense.

00:10:05.171 --> 00:10:06.972
-I have my own views
of the word socialist

00:10:06.972 --> 00:10:09.975
and I'll be glad to tell them,
share them with you in private.

00:10:09.975 --> 00:10:12.211
[ Laughter ]
And they go back
to the early 1950s.

00:10:12.211 --> 00:10:13.679
I have an attitude about them.

00:10:13.679 --> 00:10:14.846
I remember the Cold War.

00:10:14.846 --> 00:10:16.749
I have an attitude
towards Castro.

00:10:16.749 --> 00:10:20.219
I believe, if Castro and the
reds had won the Cold War,

00:10:20.219 --> 00:10:22.421
there would have been
executions in Central Park

00:10:22.421 --> 00:10:24.856
and I might've been one
of the ones getting executed.

00:10:24.856 --> 00:10:27.492
And certain other people
would be there, cheering, okay?

00:10:27.492 --> 00:10:29.595
So I have a problem with people
who took the other side.

00:10:29.595 --> 00:10:33.065
I don't know who Bernie
supports over these years.

00:10:33.065 --> 00:10:34.633
I don't know what he means
by socialism.

00:10:34.633 --> 00:10:36.369
One week, it's Denmark.

00:10:36.369 --> 00:10:37.502
We're gonna be like Denmark.

00:10:37.502 --> 00:10:39.304
Okay. That's harmless.

00:10:39.304 --> 00:10:40.639
It's basically
a capitalist country

00:10:40.639 --> 00:10:42.741
with a lotta good
social welfare programs.

00:10:42.741 --> 00:10:44.376
Denmark is harmless.
-He's pretty clearly

00:10:44.376 --> 00:10:46.178
in the Denmark category.
-Is he?

00:10:46.178 --> 00:10:47.279
-Yeah.
-Are you sure? How do you know?

00:10:47.279 --> 00:10:48.313
Did he tell you that?

00:10:48.313 --> 00:10:49.548
-Well, I mean,
that's what he says

00:10:49.548 --> 00:10:50.983
and that's what his agenda
calls for.

00:10:50.983 --> 00:10:53.986
-Just as a reminder, that whole
thing started with this...

00:10:53.986 --> 00:10:55.787
-I have my own views
of the word socialist

00:10:55.787 --> 00:10:58.457
and I'll be glad to tell them,
share them with you in private.

00:10:58.457 --> 00:11:00.526
[ Laughter ]

00:11:00.526 --> 00:11:02.161
-Chris Matthews
is definitely a guy

00:11:02.161 --> 00:11:04.129
who says he'll share his
thoughts with you in private

00:11:04.129 --> 00:11:06.398
and then talks to you in public
for a full minute.

00:11:06.398 --> 00:11:07.933
[ Laughter and applause ]
[as Matthews] I'll tell you

00:11:07.933 --> 00:11:09.735
what I think about this movie
later, in private.

00:11:09.735 --> 00:11:11.169
It sucks!

00:11:11.169 --> 00:11:12.872
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:11:12.872 --> 00:11:14.139
By the way,
Bernie is not the first

00:11:14.139 --> 00:11:15.841
strong progressive candidate
to come under fire

00:11:15.841 --> 00:11:18.244
from centrist pundits in the
Democratic establishment.

00:11:18.244 --> 00:11:19.945
When Elizabeth Warren
was soaring in the polls

00:11:19.945 --> 00:11:21.280
and seen as the front-runner,

00:11:21.280 --> 00:11:23.449
we got story after story
about how Wall Street

00:11:23.449 --> 00:11:24.883
and Democratic donors
were panicking.

00:11:24.883 --> 00:11:27.419
Cable news shows rolled
one clip after another

00:11:27.419 --> 00:11:29.488
of billionaires freaking out
about her plans.

00:11:29.488 --> 00:11:31.657
And that's because they perceive
both Bernie and Warren

00:11:31.657 --> 00:11:33.826
as threats to their livelihoods
and their way of thinking.

00:11:33.826 --> 00:11:36.561
Regardless of how you feel
about any particular candidates,

00:11:36.561 --> 00:11:38.597
if you're a pundit,
you might wanna ask

00:11:38.597 --> 00:11:41.299
why so many voters are flocking
to Bernie Sanders and, yet,

00:11:41.299 --> 00:11:43.268
when you ask them if they're
at least curious

00:11:43.268 --> 00:11:46.839
to find out why Bernie
is doing so well, they say...

00:11:46.839 --> 00:11:48.140
-Who cares?

00:11:48.140 --> 00:11:49.174
[ Laughter ]
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:11:49.174 --> 00:11:51.009
♪♪
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:11:51.009 --> 00:11:53.112
♪♪
[ Whistling ]

